<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="033" project="reuse-governance-tightening-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Execute the owner-approved decision for @spaarke/document-operations</title>
    <phase>4 Package reviews</phase>
    <gate>blocked until 032</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies .ts/.tsx code across three consumers and tests; high-risk item in the plan's risk register</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Cross-cutting migration across 3 consumers, one of them a shared package (Compose), and possibly into PCF-consumed ui-components</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>touches .claude/ (ADR-012 census) and shares src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/package.json with 031 and 032</parallel-reason>
    <deps>032</deps>
    <tags>typescript, refactoring, migration, testing</tags>
    <estimated-effort>4 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Carry out the decision recorded for @spaarke/document-operations in notes/package-reviews.md (the hypothesis is consolidation into @spaarke/ui-components), migrating all three consumers and keeping the ADR-012 census and SharedPackageCensusTests in agreement.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in the shared TypeScript packages, React 16/17 vs 19 compatibility and the ADR-012 census.</role>
  <goal>The document-operations action is complete; SpaarkeAi, the SemanticSearch code page and Compose.Components build and pass their tests; SharedPackageCensusTests passes.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>spec.md FR-09. Consumers (verified 2026-11-10): src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/package.json line 47, src/client/code-pages/SemanticSearch/package.json line 18, src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/package.json line 38. The package holds open-in-Word, download and delete hooks with abstracted I/O, the same contract as ui-components. Memory note: SemanticSearch and DocumentRelationshipViewer must share document UI via @spaarke/ui-components.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.DocumentOperations</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/index.ts</file>
      <file role="modify">src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/package.json</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/code-pages/SemanticSearch/package.json</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/package.json</file>
      <file role="modify">.claude/adr/ADR-012-shared-components.md</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/SharedPackageCensusTests.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/reuse-governance-tightening-r1/notes/package-reviews.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="032" status="pending">Serialises edits to SpaarkeAi package.json and the census</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-012">The census row and SharedPackageCensusTests entry change in the same commit as the package change.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-012">Code moved into ui-components uses runtime-context abstractions only (no ComponentFramework.*, no direct Xrm.WebApi), exports its types, and ships its tests.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-022">Every hook or component moved into ui-components is React 16/17-compatible: no useTransition, no useDeferredValue, no React 18/19-only APIs; verify by Grep on the moved files.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Tests move with the code; cover the existing contract only, or justify extras in one line in notes.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Run conflict-check before editing SpaarkeAi and Compose (compose projects are active). Use npm install --legacy-peer-deps --no-audit --no-fund.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">If ui-components' PCF bundle grows, record the before/after size of one PCF consumer build in notes.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-012-shared-components.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-022-pcf-platform-libraries.md</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/testing.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/testing/unit-test-structure.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/testing/mocking-patterns.md</file>
      <file>.claude/skills/conflict-check/SKILL.md</file>
      <file>projects/reuse-governance-tightening-r1/notes/package-reviews.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Shared package exports" location="src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/index.ts">Barrel exports for the sanctioned package.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Read the document-operations section and owner decision; run conflict-check.</step>
    <step order="2">Apply the decision: move code and tests, update the target barrel, migrate all three consumers' package.json, imports, aliases and build config.</step>
    <step order="3">Update the ADR-012 census row and SharedPackageCensusTests in the same change.</step>
    <step order="4">Build and test ui-components, Compose.Components, SemanticSearch and SpaarkeAi; run the SharedPackageCensus ArchTests.</step>
    <step order="5">Update TASK-INDEX.md: change this task's status cell to `✅ [done]`.</step>
    <step order="6">Record deviations, bundle sizes and defects found in projects/reuse-governance-tightening-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If a moved hook needs a React 18+ API, STOP and escalate (ADR-022) rather than rewriting its behaviour.</trigger>
    <trigger>If a PCF consumer build of ui-components fails or grows by more than 10%, STOP and report to the owner before continuing.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools>
    <tool name="npm">npm install --legacy-peer-deps --no-audit --no-fund; npm run build; npm test</tool>
    <tool name="dotnet">dotnet test tests/Spaarke.ArchTests --filter SharedPackageCensus</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/index.ts</output>
    <output type="code">src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/package.json</output>
    <output type="code">src/client/code-pages/SemanticSearch/package.json</output>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/package.json</output>
    <output type="docs">.claude/adr/ADR-012-shared-components.md</output>
    <output type="test">tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/SharedPackageCensusTests.cs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">The owner-approved action is fully applied across all three consumers.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">ui-components, Compose.Components, SemanticSearch and SpaarkeAi build, and their existing tests pass.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">SharedPackageCensusTests passes; census row and test entry match.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: after consolidate/retire, Grep finds no @spaarke/document-operations reference in src/.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: the moved files contain no useTransition or useDeferredValue.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Cover the existing contract only; extras justified in one line in notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Item 4 PR(s) are separate from the items 1-3 PR (NFR-05).</notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Before starting, load all files listed in &lt;knowledge&gt;&lt;files&gt;. Follow task-execute for the pre-execution checklist.</protocol>
  </execution>
</task>
